{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Background The following systematic review explores the uses and understandings of physical, human-to-human touch engagements in healthcare professions. Given its central importance as both a diagnostic tool and a form of non-verbal communication, this review sought to understand the communicative, social and affective dimensions of touches a part of healthcare, medical or nursing interventions.",
      "reason": "The abstract/background describes the current state (central importance of touch as diagnostic tool and non-verbal communication) and sets the focus on communicative, social and affective dimensions, indicating the knowledge area and implicitly pointing to gaps the review addresses."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "In light of this brief background analysis, the present review sets itself apart from previous ones by attempting to understand the communicative, social and affective dimensions of touch in healthcare and nursing professions, in both its instrumental and expressive instances.",
      "reason": "The introduction/Aim explains the importance and need for this review by stating how it differs from prior work and by articulating the review's purpose to investigate communicative, social and affective dimensions, justifying why the review is needed."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "In light of this brief background analysis, the present review sets itself apart from previous ones by attempting to understand the communicative, social and affective dimensions of touch in healthcare and nursing professions, in both its instrumental and expressive instances.",
      "reason": "The manuscript acknowledges prior reviews and states this review 'sets itself apart from previous ones', but it does not identify, cite, or describe specific similar systematic reviews or explicitly explain the need as an update or replication of particular prior reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "For instance, studies such as those of [54, 55] and [56] initially appeared to respond to the question posed by the present review; upon a closer appraisal however, they were all excluded because they focused solely on assessing the functional dynamics and efficacy of touch interventions, without exploring the impact of such a touch experience on either the practitioner or the patient.",
      "reason": "The review explicitly excludes studies that focus on intervention efficacy and is exploratory rather than an effects review; therefore describing a mechanism of action for interventions is not applicable."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "A PICo (Population, Interest, Context) framework ([45]; see also: [46]) was used to formulate the preliminary question 'What are care-givers' (i.e. allied health professionals, nurses, doctors, carers) [Population] actual uses and experiences of touch [Interest] when providing real and direct medical care to patients [Context]?' .",
      "reason": "The review focuses on understanding uses and experiences of touch rather than evaluating a complex intervention or its delivery; thus a logic model for intervention components and outcomes is not applicable."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

