      "reason": "The review uses a PICo framework for an exploratory synthesis of uses/experiences of touch rather than reviewing intervention effects; thus planned PICO comparisons for interventions do not apply."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Both qualitative and quantitative studies were considered eligible, but non-empirical studies were not ('non-empirical' exclusion criterion). No specific sociometric variables (e.g. sex, age, socioeconomic status of participants) were sought, and studies were not excluded on the basis of their design (e.g. number of participants, methods).",
      "reason": "The excerpt explicitly states eligible study designs (qualitative and quantitative), exclusion of non-empirical studies, and that no specific participant sociodemographic variables or design-based exclusions were applied, addressing key study characteristics used to determine eligibility."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "The present review is exploratory in nature: for this reason, studies from all years and in any language spoken by the team (i.e. English, Italian, French, Spanish, Finnish) were included ('Language' exclusion criterion).",
      "reason": "The excerpt specifies language inclusion (and the languages covered) and that studies from all years were included; publication/report status is addressed via exclusion of non-empirical reports in the same section (see table_0), satisfying report-characteristic eligibility reporting."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No explicit statement distinguishing exclusion because outcomes were not measured from exclusion because outcome results were not reported was found in the provided evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "descriptive themes were connected into 4 higher-level analytical themes.",
      "reason": "The review reports that studies were grouped into descriptive themes and then four higher-level analytical themes for synthesis (showing how studies were grouped), but the provided evidence does not explicitly link these groups to specific comparisons defined in the review objectives."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Two of them ('language' and 'non-empirical') were based on the team expertise and the general aim of this review (i.e. capturing empirical social analysis over anecdotal case studies or philosophical discussions), while the other 8 were formulated starting from the PICo framework.",
      "reason": "The excerpt provides explicit rationale for notable eligibility restrictions (e.g. why language and non-empirical exclusions were applied), explaining their justification in relation to team expertise and review aims."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "85"
}

